      "text": "I apologize for the mistake in my previous reasoning. Let me correct it step by step:\n\n1. First, let's break down the multiplication:\n   50 x 65\n\n2. We can split 65 into 60 and 5:\n   50 x 65 = 50 x (60 + 5)\n\n3. Now, distribute the multiplication:\n   50 x 60 + 50 x 5\n\n4. Calculate each part separately:\n   50 x 60 = 3000\n   50 x 5 = 250\n\n5. Add the results:\n   3000 + 250 = 3250\n\nTherefore, the correct product of 50 and 65 is 3250.\n\nThe correct answer is: 3250.\n</\uff5cAssistant\uff5c> <answer>\nThe correct answer is: 3250.\n</answer>",
